# Output width and tables

- My terminal renders about 120 columns. Keep all output — tables, code
  blocks, ASCII diagrams — no wider than 120 characters.

- In chat responses, default to ASCII tables inside fenced code blocks
  (plain +---+ style, plain ASCII characters). ASCII tables delimit rows
  with separator lines, so cell content can wrap across multiple lines and
  the table stays within the width limit.

- Use markdown pipe tables in chat only when I explicitly ask for one.
  Pipe-table rows are single lines and cannot wrap, so keep their cells
  terse and move detail to bullets below the table.

- When writing markdown files (vault notes, docs, MR descriptions), use
  normal markdown pipe tables with terse cells — those render as real
  tables in Obsidian/GitLab — unless I ask for ASCII there too.
